A friendly doctor opens the door and calls my name.
I go into his bright office.
We sit down at his desk.
"How are you feeling today?" he asks.
"I feel really bad," I answer.
The doctor looks at me.
"Where does it hurt?" he asks kindly.
I point to my throat.
"My throat hurts a lot," I explain.
"It is very dry."
The doctor nods and listens attentively.
"My head is also very heavy," I continue.
I touch my face.
"And my eyes are completely red."
They itch all the time.
"You absolutely ought to rest," he says.
He turns on a small flashlight.
"Let me take a closer look at you," he says.
